Aether: accounts and Normandy out

Firefox Accounts UI, sync promos and widgets, Normandy and its newtab fallout.

Squashed from 4 units:

  [core/105-no-firefox-accounts.patch]
  Aether: remove the Firefox Accounts surface
  
  Remove the Firefox Accounts surface: the about:logins sign-in button and sync state, the protections Monitor/VPN OAuth flows (static no-account answers), `FxAccountsCommon` and the services dir, the AI logout observer and token backend, the orphaned synced-tabs sidebar and its menus, startup `AccountsGlue`, the IPProtection FxA provider, the Kinto storage backend, messaging and tour sign-in flows, the welcome sign-in buttons and device-migration screen, the share-panel device flows, dead toolbar placements and prefs, orphaned tests and strings. Untouched by design: the audited-inert guarded paths (opentabs, sidebar-opentabs, PrivacyFeed, RemoteTabs, PlacesUIUtils, BackupService, ASRouter targeting names) and the degrading `AIWindowAccountAuth` module.
  
  [core/106-no-sync-promos-widgets.patch]
  Aether: remove the sync promos, widgets and send-to-device UI
  
  Remove the sync promos (places, appmenu), the sync/send-tab toolbar widgets, the MenuMessage account-panel force-show, the tab context send-to-device updater, and the sync-promo element with its registration. The guarded promo branch in places stays: it can never execute without accounts.
  
  [core/107-no-normandy.patch]
  Aether: remove Normandy (keep Nimbus local)
  
  Remove Normandy via its own build flag (MOZ_NORMANDY off): the component, its startup/quit hooks, the extension study API, and every consumer rewired to local UUIDs (Nimbus, targeting, troubleshoot, tests). Nimbus stays as a local feature-flag reader with its remote loader already neutered. Untouched by design: flag-gated FirstStartup/Troubleshoot paths, inert prefs, and test files that only skip on the flag.\n
  
  [core/108-no-normandy-newtab-fallout.patch]
  Aether: ungate newtab startup from Nimbus and drop dead Glean sites
  
  With Normandy gone (107) nothing calls ExperimentAPI.init() in production,
  so the ExperimentStore SharedDataMap never resolves ready(). AboutNewTab
  waited on that promise before creating ActivityStream, hanging newtab
  startup forever: activityStream stayed null, content never received state
  and about:newtab rendered blank (plus a requestCache TypeError on the null
  stream at shutdown). Do not gate newtab startup on Nimbus anymore; trainhop
  config falls back to local preference defaults, which is all Aether ships.
  
  Same cascade in DevTools: the loader injected a `Glean` global that no
  longer exists, so any DevTools shortcut threw ReferenceError and the
  browser console stayed dead; drop it from the sandbox globals (this also
  fixes the derived `lazy.Telemetry is not a constructor` failure).
  
  Also drop the last live Glean site on the newtab path: the resource-mapping
  helper referenced the deleted NewTabGleanUtils module (only reachable from
  the XPI trainhop branch, which can no longer enroll anything).
